@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Explicit Drive ZIP transfers, independent of local saving
autonumber
actor Author
participant "TransferService\nC#" as T
participant "Google OAuth / Picker\nbrowser glue" as Auth
participant "Drive adapter\nC#" as Adapter
participant "Google Drive" as Drive
participant "ProjectRepository" as Repo
Author -> T : explicit import or export
T -> Auth : obtain user-granted drive.file access
alt consent denied / authorization unavailable
  Auth --> T : AuthenticationRequired / denied
  T --> Author : transfer stopped; local project unaffected
else authorized
  Auth --> T : memory-only access token / selection
  alt export local revision R
    T -> Repo : capture immutable snapshot R
    Repo --> T : exact revision contents
    T -> T : build ZIP; exclude secrets / caches / chat
    T -> Adapter : export as NEW Drive file
    Adapter -> Drive : upload ZIP snapshot R
    Drive --> Adapter : file receipt or typed failure
    Adapter --> T : transfer status for R
  else import selected ZIP
    T -> Adapter : download selected file
    Adapter -> Drive : explicit download
    Drive --> Adapter : ZIP bytes or failure
    alt download failed
      Adapter --> T : typed failure; no staged import
    else complete ZIP received
      Adapter --> T : staged content
      T -> T : validate paths / archive limits / settings
      opt replacing existing local project
        T --> Author : request replacement confirmation
        Author -> T : accept or cancel
        T -> Repo : preserve checkpoint if accepted
      end
      opt valid and accepted import
        T -> Repo : commit new revision / project; head check
        Repo --> T : locally committed or storage failure
      end
    end
  end
  T --> Author : separate transfer / local-save statuses
end
note over T, Drive
Expiry or network failure requires explicit retry / reauthorization.
No background upload, autosync or existing-Drive-file overwrite.
Failed download never enters local commit.
end note
@enduml
